{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-101413",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We know that $a⊥b$ ($a$ and $b$ are perpendicular) if and only if $a\\cdot b=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot 4+5\\cdot x \\\\  & =-6x-4+5x \\\\  & =-x-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ -x-4 & =0 \\\\ x & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
